<title>MEXICO: Bital Grupo Financiero Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Bital Grupo Financiero Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			  1995</p>
<p>     Shr		 0.3054		   0.074</p>
<p>     Oper Income     n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>     Net		 157.37 million	     38.11</p>
<p>     Revs		n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>	 NOTE: All figures in Mexican pesos.</p>
<p>	 Full company name is Bital Grupo Financiero SA de CV.</p>
<p>	 The company also gave the following nine-month results:</p>
<p>				   1996			  1995</p>
<p>     Shr		 n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>     Oper Income     n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>     Net		 425.21 million	     45.03 million</p>
<p>     Revs		n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>	 NOTE: The group gave the following data for its banking</p>
<p>unit Banco Internacional SA 's contribution to results. The group has a 96.83 percent stake in the bank.</p>
<p>Third quarter</p>
<p>     Net		 113.65 million	     34.6 million</p>
<p>Nine months</p>
<p>     Net		 298.86 million	     58.48 million</p>
<p>	 NOTE: The company said Banco Internacional's</p>
<p>capitalisation ratio at the end of September 1996 was 14.1 percent and reserve coverage for past-due loans was 100.1 percent. The bank created bad-loan reserves of 220 million pesos in the third quarter, charged against results.</p>
<p>--Mexico City newsroom 525 7289500</p>
</text>
